<https://hexplain.io/ns/core> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Properties linking the physical, layout, and semantic layers of the Hexplain framework."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ClassMappingRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A rule selecting the owl:Class a bddo:Struct represents based on a discriminator condition; used in a hexplain:hasConditionalClassMapping list to model tagged unions / variant records."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ClassMappingRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ClassMappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:condition, hexplain:semanticClass. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ClassMappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of hexplain:ClassMappingRule Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ClassMappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Class Mapping Rule Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ClassMappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#CodecParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A named setting of a codec. Deliberately a name/value pair rather than a fixed vocabulary: codec options are open-ended and vendor-specific, and enumerating them would date immediately."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#CodecParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#CodecParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:parameterName, hexplain:parameterValue. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#CodecParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of hexplain:CodecParameter Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#CodecParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Codec Parameter Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#CodecParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingPipelineShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:hasEncodingStep. Every member of a hasEncodingStep list must be a hexplain:EncodingStep. hexplain:hasEncodingStep must point to a single rdf:List."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingPipelineShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:hasEncodingStep Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingPipelineShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Encoding Pipeline Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingPipelineShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One stage of an encoding pipeline: a codec, plus the parameters it was applied with."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingStepShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:codec, hexplain:codecParameter. An encoding step must name exactly one codec."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingStepShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of hexplain:EncodingStep Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingStepShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Encoding Step Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#EncodingStepShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalClassMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:mapsToClass. Every member of a hasConditionalClassMapping list must be a hexplain:ClassMappingRule. hexplain:mapsToClass and hexplain:hasConditionalClassMapping are mutually exclusive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalClassMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:hasConditionalClassMapping Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalClassMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Has Conditional Class Mapping Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalClassMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Has Conditional Mapping. Every member of a hasConditionalMapping list must be a hexplain:MappingRule."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:hasConditionalMapping Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Has Conditional Mapping Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasConditionalMappingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasDataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:hasDataLayout. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasDataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:hasDataLayout Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasDataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Has Data Layout Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#HasDataLayoutShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#IsEncodedWithShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:hasEncodingStep, hexplain:isEncodedWith. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#IsEncodedWithShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:isEncodedWith Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#IsEncodedWithShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is Encoded With Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#IsEncodedWithShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageFromFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:languageFromField. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageFromFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:languageFromField Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageFromFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Language From Field Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageFromFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:language, hexplain:languageFromField. hexplain:language and hexplain:languageFromField are mutually exclusive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:language Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Language Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#LanguageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MappingRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A rule for conditionally mapping a physical field to a semantic property."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MappingRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:condition, hexplain:semanticProperty, hexplain:valueDatatype, hexplain:valueExpression. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of hexplain:MappingRule Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mapping Rule Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MappingRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToClassShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:mapsToClass. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToClassShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:mapsToClass Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToClassShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Maps To Class Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToClassShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToObjectPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:mapsToObjectProperty. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToObjectPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:mapsToObjectProperty Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToObjectPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Maps To Object Property Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToObjectPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:mapsToProperty. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:mapsToProperty Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Maps To Property Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#MapsToPropertyShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A statement that one property draws its values from one controlled register."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Register Binding. Value {?value} of {?p} is not skos:inScheme the declared register {?scheme}."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: No automatic target; applied only when another shape references it or a caller explicitly selects it. Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Register Binding Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#UnitShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:unit. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#UnitShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:unit Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#UnitShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unit Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#UnitShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ValueExpressionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for hexplain:valueDatatype, hexplain:valueExpression. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ValueExpressionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:valueExpression Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ValueExpressionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Value Expression Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#ValueExpressionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Namespace prefix declarations reused by SHACL SPARQL constraints and rules. This is validation infrastructure, not a property of parsed data."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used by named SHACL SPARQL constraints/rules in this module. Not intended for instance-data assertions."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "prefixes"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/core> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codec> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The algorithm this step applies, drawn from whichever codec or compression register the profile binds -- the same registers hexplain:isEncodedWith draws on."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codec> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codecParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A named parameter value associated with one stage of an encoding pipeline."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codecParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A HEL boolean condition selecting a semantic mapping or conditional class mapping in its declared context."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#forProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The semantic RDF predicate whose controlled-value register binding is declared by this binding resource."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#forProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalClassMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of hexplain:ClassMappingRule on a bddo:Struct. The class the Struct maps to is the hexplain:semanticClass of the first rule whose hexplain:condition holds — modelling tagged unions and variant records, where a record's type depends on a discriminator field. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:mapsToClass."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalClassMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ordered list of mapping rules that choose a semantic property according to the parsed instance."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasDataLayout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Field to a dlv:DataLayout describing its multi-dimensional interpretation."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasDataLayout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasEncodingStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of EncodingStep, in the order the ENCODER applied them; a decoder inverts them in reverse. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:isEncodedWith, which remains the shorthand for a single unparameterised codec."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasEncodingStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#isEncodedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The algorithm needed to interpret a data block, drawn from whichever codec or compression register the profile binds. A processor decodes the block, then re-parses the decoded bytes against the field's data type when it is a bddo:Struct."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#isEncodedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#language> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fixed BCP-47 language tag applied to the string literal emitted for a bddo:Field, producing a language-tagged literal. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:languageFromField."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#language> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#languageFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bddo:Field whose parsed string value supplies the BCP-47 language tag for this field's emitted string literal, for formats that carry a text run's language in a sibling field. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:language."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#languageFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Struct to the owl:Class it physically represents."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToObjectProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Field to the owl:ObjectProperty whose object is an IRI rather than a literal: the resource minted for a nested Struct instance (when the field's bddo:dataType is a bddo:Struct) or the field's enumeration symbol IRI (when it carries a bddo:enumeration whose bddo:enumSymbol values are IRIs). Use hexplain:mapsToProperty for literal-valued fields and this property for IRI-valued edges, so that a described format yields a connected RDF graph rather than isolated literals."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToObjectProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Field to the rdf:Property it supplies a value for."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The setting's name as the codec itself names it: \"clevel\", \"shuffle\", \"predictor\"."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The setting's value, as the literal the format carries. Left untyped: a level is an integer, a Blosc inner codec a string, a flag a boolean."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#register> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The skos:ConceptScheme whose members are the permitted values."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#register> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The owl:Class selected by a hexplain:ClassMappingRule when its condition holds."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The RDF property selected by a matching semantic mapping rule."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The unit of measure of the quantity a bddo:Field carries, as an IRI drawn from a unit vocabulary (e.g. QUDT or UCUM; the range is skos:Concept but any unit IRI is permitted). Annotation only: it records the physical unit of the emitted value and does not rescale it — use hexplain:valueExpression for numeric conversion."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#usesRegister> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Binds a property used by this profile to the register supplying its values."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#usesRegister> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueDatatype> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The xsd datatype of a computed hexplain:valueExpression result; defaults to the natural datatype of the HEL result type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueDatatype> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A HEL expression computing the value to emit for the mapped property instead of the field's raw parsed value (e.g. fixed-point or unit scaling). Evaluated in the field's context."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use when linking a physical format description to semantic RDF output, encoding stages or controlled-value bindings. It does not replace the byte-layout description. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
